# Backend Patterns — REST

APIs must follow REST constraints and HTTP semantics. Nest structure: module → controller → service → (repository).

## URLs & resources

- Plural nouns: `/users`, `/posts/{id}` — not `/getUser`, `/user_list`
- Nest: `@Controller('users')` — no trailing slash; lowercase kebab-case
- Sub-resources: `/users/{userId}/posts`
- Version when breaking: `/v1/users` or header `Accept-Version`

## HTTP methods & status

| Method  | Use              | Success codes        |
| ------- | ---------------- | -------------------- |
| GET     | Read (safe)      | 200, 204             |
| POST    | Create           | 201 + `Location`     |
| PUT     | Full replace     | 200, 204             |
| PATCH   | Partial update   | 200                  |
| DELETE  | Remove           | 204, 200             |

- ✅ `201` + body or `Location` on create; ✅ `404` missing resource; ✅ `422`/`400` validation
- ❌ `200` on DELETE of missing id without consistency; ❌ verbs in path (`/users/create`)

## Representation

- JSON request/response; `Content-Type: application/json`
- DTOs + `class-validator` / `ValidationPipe` on input
- Stable field names; ISO 8601 dates; never leak stack traces in prod

## Stateless & errors

- No server session for API auth state; use tokens if auth is added
- Map domain errors to HTTP via Nest exceptions (`NotFoundException`, `BadRequestException`)
- Consistent error body: `{ statusCode, message, error? }` (Nest default) or documented shape

## Controllers vs services

- Controller: routing, status, headers, DTO binding — no business rules
- Service: domain logic, transactions, persistence

```typescript
// ✅ REST controller
@Controller('users')
export class UsersController {
  @Post()
  @HttpCode(HttpStatus.CREATED)
  create(@Body() dto: CreateUserDto) { /* ... */ }

  @Get(':id')
  findOne(@Param('id', ParseUUIDPipe) id: string) { /* ... */ }
}
```

- ❌ `GET /users/delete/{id}`; ❌ RPC-style `@Post('doSomething')` unless truly non-resource action (document exception)
